---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Membership Terms"
  description="Arizona Pole Vault Academy membership terms for Elite and Lite club members — billing, cancellation, poles, parking, and reservations."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Policies</p>
      <h1>Membership Terms</h1>
      <p style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.85)">
        Arizona Pole Vault Academy, Inc. — Elite and Lite club memberships.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      
      
      
      <h2>1. Minors</h2>
      <p>If you are under 18, a parent or legal guardian must agree to these terms on your behalf.</p>
      
      <h2>2. Month-to-month membership</h2>
      <p>Elite and Lite club memberships are <strong>month-to-month</strong>. There is no long-term contract.</p>
      
      <p>Once your initial payment is received and your membership has started, you are committed for that month. Each month’s commitment applies regardless of illness, injury, vacation, or other circumstances.</p>
      
      <p>Memberships <strong>auto-renew</strong> until canceled. It is your responsibility to cancel before the next billing period.</p>
      
      <h2>3. Payment methods</h2>
      <ul class="list-check">
      <li>Club memberships: **credit card only**</li>
      <li>Camps: credit card, **cash, or check** also accepted</li>
      </ul>
      
      <h2>4. Changes and cancellation</h2>
      <p>To change, pause by canceling, or cancel your membership, send <strong>written notice at least 2 days before the end of the month</strong>, and wait for our <strong>confirmation</strong>, so the next credit-card charge can be stopped.</p>
      
      <p>Written notice must be sent to <strong>arizonapolevaultacademy@gmail.com</strong> or by text to <strong>(480) 766-6017</strong>.  </p>
      <p>If we have not confirmed, we did not receive your message.</p>
      
      <p>Failure to cancel within the allowed time results in a <strong>$25 late-cancellation fee</strong> (card processing and administrative costs).</p>
      
      <h2>5. Upgrades and downgrades</h2>
      <p>You may upgrade or downgrade without penalty.</p>
      
      <ul class="list-check">
      <li>**Upgrade at next billing cycle:** new plan starts then at the full new rate.</li>
      <li>**Upgrade immediately:** remaining days in the current cycle are prorated at the new rate; the next monthly bill is the full new rate.</li>
      <li>**Downgrade:** takes effect on the next monthly bill date (not retroactive).</li>
      </ul>
      
      <h2>6. Refunds</h2>
      <p>If you forgot to cancel and you have <strong>not attended</strong> any session in that period, you may request a refund within <strong>7 days</strong>. A <strong>$25 late-cancellation fee</strong> still applies. After 7 days, the membership fee is non-refundable.</p>
      
      <h2>7. Pausing</h2>
      <p>We do not pause memberships. To take time off, cancel at the end of a month and use drop-ins if needed.</p>
      
      <h2>8. Prorating</h2>
      <p>Prorating is case-by-case. It is typically offered for a <strong>first-time</strong> signup mid-month. We do not prorate for vacations, illness, or similar circumstances.</p>
      
      <h2>9. Attendance</h2>
      <p>Attendance is encouraged but not mandatory.</p>
      
      <h2>10. Weather</h2>
      <p>Sessions may be canceled for unsafe weather. We typically decide about <strong>one hour</strong> before start and notify the contact info on the <strong>member account profile</strong> by email and/or SMS.</p>
      
      <p><strong>Important:</strong> Parent/guardian proxy accounts may not receive weather notices due to system limits. Put a reachable mobile number on the athlete/member profile used for messaging.</p>
      
      <p>There are <strong>no make-up sessions</strong> for weather cancellations.</p>
      
      <h2>11. Practice schedules</h2>
      <p>We aim to keep days/times consistent and to publish the next month’s schedule before the month begins. Track season and coaching travel may require changes; we will communicate as quickly as possible.</p>
      
      <p>We typically schedule <strong>3 sessions per week</strong>, with <strong>one Saturday off per month</strong>.</p>
      
      <h2>12. Driving and parking</h2>
      <p>Drive cautiously in the neighborhood (posted limit 25 mph; please keep closer to <strong>20</strong>). Keep stereo volume low.</p>
      
      <ul class="list-check">
      <li>Park down the driveway on the **right** toward the barn; pull all the way forward.</li>
      <li>You may park outside the barn or in the horse arena if gates are open. Do **not** block the arena entrance.</li>
      <li>If the back is full, you may park in front of our house or by our horse trailers.</li>
      <li>**Never** park in front of neighbors’ houses or in the open area on the west side of the property (not ours).</li>
      <li>**Drop-off / pick-up:** in front of the house only. Do not drive down the driveway for drop-off/pick-up (backs up traffic / hard to turn around).</li>
      </ul>
      
      <h2>13. Borrowing poles (Elite only)</h2>
      <ul class="list-check">
      <li>Only **Elite** members may borrow poles (up to **3**) for competitions. Lite members may not borrow; Lite may arrange rentals separately.</li>
      <li>Only AZPVA Elite members may vault on checked-out poles. Sharing with non-Elite athletes is prohibited.</li>
      <li>Checkout after the late practice session; return **15 minutes before** the next early practice unless a coach approves otherwise.</li>
      <li>Lost, stolen, or damaged poles must be replaced at manufacturer retail (typically about **$350–$700** each).</li>
      <li>Late same-day return: **$10 per pole**. Returned a day late: treated as rented at **$25 per pole per day**.</li>
      <li>Care: protective bag in transport/competition; never leave exposed on the ground; pad standards if the pole can strike them; return with plug or **$10** charge. Privileges may be revoked for policy violations.</li>
      <li>Off-hours drop-off: call/text Dean at **(480) 766-6017** before leaving poles on the north side of the garage.</li>
      </ul>
      
      <h2>14. Class reservations</h2>
      <ul class="list-check">
      <li>Reserve in the member app up to **7 days** ahead, until **1 hour** before start.</li>
      <li>Cancel in the app as soon as you know you will miss.</li>
      <li>Cancel up to **60 minutes** before start without late-cancel flag; within 60 minutes = late cancel.</li>
      <li>Multiple no-shows or late cancels may temporarily suspend booking of popular sessions.</li>
      <li>More than **15 minutes** late without notice: your spot may be given to the waitlist.</li>
      </ul>
      
      <h2>15. Agreement</h2>
      <p>To become an Elite or Lite club member, you must agree to these terms.</p>
      
      <p><strong>Agreement:</strong> To become an Elite or Lite club member, you must agree to these terms.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
